<Step id="STEP_3B_TOOL_API">
      <Goal>`config` kind only: verify each configured third-party tool through the declared ecosystem's registered ToolDocAdapter (`AX_THIRD_PARTY_TOOL_CURRENT_API`). Any other kind skips this step.</Goal>
      <Action>
        <ToolDocAdapterRegistry>
          Activate only when STEP_1 `phaseContext.kind=config`; every other kind skips without a
          probe. Detect ecosystem + tool only from that phaseContext's Target Files, Spec Refs, and
          readiness evidence — never memory, repo-wide search, or filename guessing. Each adapter
          owns its version source, permitted local docs, and explicit remote policy:

          | Adapter | Version + local docs | Remote policy |
          |---|---|---|
          | `node/npm` | `node_modules/<pkg>/package.json#version`; that installed package root's `README*` and `CHANGELOG*` | only if local docs are insufficient, WebFetch the exact `homepage` or `repository.url` in that same package manifest |
          | `go` | unsupported — no registered adapter | none |
          | `ios/swift` | unsupported — no registered adapter | none |
          | `android/gradle` | unsupported — no registered adapter | none |

          An ambiguous ecosystem, unregistered tool, unsupported adapter, missing installed version,
          or insufficient permitted evidence → `H_THIRD_PARTY_API_UNVERIFIABLE`. Missing adapter,
          version, or persisted docs is `RECOVERABLE_TECHNICAL`; an exact external-access permission
          is `EXTERNAL_AUTHORITY_REQUIRED`. Return evidence and the bounded next action. Never guess, call `--help`,
          explore an undeclared cache, inspect tool internals, or access the network outside the
          selected adapter's remote policy.
        </ToolDocAdapterRegistry>

        BEFORE writing config, select and follow that adapter. Exact config specifics remain a
        decision-time infra-spec concern
        (`AX_RESEARCH_PERSISTED`, `infra.directive` STEP_3_TOOL_CHOICES), sourced from Spec Refs or a
        linked research artifact.
        Then write exact `verified <tool>@<version> <one-line summary>` to the phase log payload and
        run eventLog ToolCall below — audit requires this entry per config artifact.
        <ToolCall owner="phase-worker" result="eventLog">npx gennady sdd-log <ticket> line --content-file .claude/tmp/<task-id>-<phase-id>-log.txt --phase <PhaseID></ToolCall> Inputs <ticket>, <task-id>, <phase-id>, <PhaseID>: file-write of literal evidence gathered here. Use eventLog.
      </Action>
    </Step>